  "instructions": [
    "Rinse and drain quinoa.",
    "Combine quinoa, dates, olive oil, lemon juice, salt, pepper in a bowl. Toss to coat.",
    "Add water or broth to the bowl; cover with lid or plastic wrap and cook on medium-high heat until liquid is absorbed, about 15 minutes.",
    "Preheat donabe vessel over medium heat. Place quinoa mixture inside, seam side up.",
    "Cover with lid and bake at 375°F (190°C) for 20-25 minutes or until edges are golden brown and liquid is evaporated.",
    "Serve hot."
